in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform
in @epistemologic/math/lawvere

# @third — recursion-depth marker at substrate-decl altitude.
#
# Loki (systemic.engineering blog, "Void → Third", 2026-06-22):
#
#   Not third as apex. Third as recursive depth. The observer of
#   the observer of the observer.
#
# The substrate has been operating at third-order altitude implicitly
# for one recognition cascade (per candidate #111, Alex 2026-07-01):
#   - @reflection substrate-decl'd third_order_observation at v0.1
#     spec 2026-06-22 (Pack-ratified, 1514 lines).
#   - @cyberpunk's ceiling species is @epistemologic/cybernetic/
#     second_order (Foerster).
#   - @pack demonstrated multi-repo third-order at StageFreight
#     (Glint essay 2026-06-22-third-order-and-multi-repo.md).
#   - @cascade at every metalogue-lift altitude is Learning II per
#     Bateson (recognition #42, deutero-learning insight).
#
# What was missing: the substrate marker naming *recursion depth
# of observation* as its own typed axis. @third supplies it.
#
# === Marker, not family-root ===
#
# @third is imported the way @meta and @glass are imported. It is
# a substrate-altitude marker crossing family-roots, NOT a peer of
# @cogito / @autopoietic / @bauchladen / @algebra / @cyberpunk /
# @metalogue. Reed's initial candidate framing had @third as a
# family-root inheriting from six roots; the writing surfaced that
# recursion-depth is a *property of an observation* (marker
# altitude), not a *domain the substrate is about* (family-root
# altitude).
#
# See docs/specs/third-as-recursive-depth.md §2 for the reshape
# argument.
#
# Marker row precedents (crossing families rather than sitting
# alongside):
#
#   @meta          "operates on substrate substrate"
#   @glass         "exposes an opacity surface"
#   @epistemologic "admits verdict discipline"
#   @third (this)  "witnesses recursion at depth >= 3"
#   @labeled       "adds label dimension to a value"
#                  (added 2026-07-01 per Loki §6 Seam-ratified 17f0ee5)
#
# Families that want third-order operation opt in via `in @third`.
# @reflection, @cogito, @pack, @cyberpunk, @fate, @cascade all
# forward-promised as opt-in consumers (per canonical spec §9);
# refinement shards land per-family when substrate pull surfaces.
#
# === Ancestry ===
#
# - Bateson 1972 (Steps to an Ecology of Mind): logical-type
#   hierarchy; Learning III at recursion-depth-3.
# - Foerster 1974/1981 (Observing Systems): second-order
#   cybernetics; observer-in-the-system; ethical imperative
#   "always act to increase the number of choices" as depth-3
#   operational endpoint.
# - Kauffman 2003 (Eigenforms; Cybernetics & Human Knowing 10:3-4):
#   recursion fixed-points; identity as the object the recursion
#   stabilizes on.
# - Lawvere 1969 (Diagonal Arguments and Cartesian Closed Categories):
#   fixed-point theorem grounding hash(P^n(f)) == f at each depth.
# - Loki (systemic.engineering, 2026-06-22): "Void → Third"; the
#   depth-vs-apex inversion.
# - Alex (2026-07-01, candidate #111): the nervous-system <-> AI
#   isomorphism naming @third as substrate-decl-worthy.
# - Reed (candidate memory entry, 2026-07-01): initial framing;
#   reshaped by this writing.
#
# === Prior substrate landings ===
#
# - docs/specs/reflection-third-order-by-default-v0.1.md (Mara,
#   2026-06-22, 1514 lines, Pack-ratified): third-order at
#   @reflection altitude; the machinery this marker factors out.
# - shards/reflection.mirror: imports @cyberpunk +
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order + eigenform; carries
#   third_order_observation + third_order_coherent + notice +
#   choices_increase + pick_third_order + settle_third_order.
# - shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order.mirror: Foerster
#   substrate-decl (445 lines); ceiling of @cyberpunk per recursion-
#   lock tower audit §8.7.
# - shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.mirror: Kauffman
#   substrate-decl (309 lines); fixed-point witness across species.
# - docs/insights/2026-06-22-third-order-and-multi-repo.md (Glint):
#   Pack multi-repo third-order empirical demonstration.
# - docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-93-cogito-cognitive-
#   substrate-candidate.md: @cogito candidate (holds forward-
#   promised @third opt-in per composition map).
#
# === Spec context ===
#
# Canonical spec: docs/specs/third-as-recursive-depth.md
# Substrate decisions:
#   [[architecture-candidate-recognition-111-third-as-family-root]]
#   (Reed's initial framing; this shard reshapes per §12 findings),
#   [[architecture-bateson-logical-type-primitive]] (recognition
#   #42; Learning-level ladder this marker labels rung 3 of),
#   [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]] (each depth-n witness
#   inherits (A_n, H_n, D_n, J_n, γ_n) per §6.5),
#   [[architecture-mirror-as-expanding-hilbert-space]] (#51; H
#   dimension expansion each cascade tick fires under third-order
#   witness),
#   [[architecture-bauchladen-fate-chain-recognition-104]] (Lawvere
#   fixed-point at each depth grounds Rice-safety per §6.4),
#   [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]] (@third
#   as marker crosses form and process without inheriting either),
#   [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (53rd+ instance;
#   @meta + @glass + @epistemologic row was the pattern @third
#   joins).
#
# Related shards:
#   metalogue.mirror (the language's self-conversation; naturally
#     fires at depth >= 2, admits @third at depth >= 3);
#   reflection.mirror (the first refinement consumer; forward-
#     promised species third_order_observation <: observation_depth);
#   epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order.mirror (depth-2 substrate;
#     @third's precondition);
#   epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.mirror (fold-back fixed-point
#     machinery).
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/third.mirror`
# declares `@third` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.
#
# === Substrate-decl-honest weakenings (per spec §11) ===
#
# - Candidate #111 strength; Pack ratification pending.
# - @bateson may or may not become its own family-root; if it does,
#   this shard adds `in @bateson`; if not, current imports are
#   sufficient.
# - Rice-safety argument is structural, not formal; formal proof
#   forward-promised at docs/math/third-order/rice-safety.md.
# - Loss function signature declared; discharge derivation forward-
#   promised.
# - Species-refinement shards NOT landed this tick; each family
#   lands its own refinement when substrate pulls.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972
source @arxiv/cybernetics/foerster-1974
source @arxiv/cybernetics/kauffman-2003
source @arxiv/math/lawvere-1969

prism @third {
  focus  observation_depth
  project observation_depth
  split  observation_depth
  shift  observation_depth
  settle observation_depth
}

# === observation_depth ===
#
# The typed carrier @third exposes to consumers. Names a recursion-
# depth witness over a substrate ref (what is being observed) via a
# witness ref (the action that observes) with a reflexivity opacity
# carrier (how much of the recursion is legible).
#
# `depth: nat` is unbounded above. @third fires at depth >= 3; higher
# depths are legitimate. `depth = 4` is the observer of the observer
# of the observer of the observer — still @third-witnessed because
# the marker fires at the depth-3 threshold, not at a fixed level.
#
# `reflexivity: transparency(ref)` is a @glass opacity carrier per
# the standard discipline (loss carrier parameterized on ref). Not
# every level of the recursion is fully legible; the marker admits
# partial legibility. Substrate-pull-honest: fully legible depth-3
# would be `partial(1.00)` = complete transparency; partial(0.85) =
# 85% inspectable.
type observation_depth = {
  depth: nat,
  substrate: ref,
  witness: ref,
  reflexivity: transparency(ref),
}

# === depth_at_least(d, o) predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict predicate — does the observation's recorded
# depth meet or exceed d? The primitive on which the composed
# third_order_active bilateral rests. Discharges via integer
# comparison + substrate resolution + reflexivity carrier
# admissibility.
#
# Same shape as @cyberpunk's cybernetic_coherence, @glass's
# transparency check — a `requires` clause consumer families cite.
depth_at_least(d: nat, o: observation_depth) -> verdict { \ }

# === observer_observes_observing(o) predicate ===
#
# The Foerster requirement: depth-2 machinery is present under the
# depth-3 witness. Discharges via @epistemologic/cybernetic/
# second_order.second_order_witnessing on o.witness — the depth-3
# observation must carry a valid depth-2 substrate.
#
# Presupposes depth_at_least(2, o). Required by third_order_active.
observer_observes_observing(o: observation_depth) -> verdict { \ }

# === recursion_folds_back(o) predicate ===
#
# The Kauffman requirement: the observation returns to the observer
# as data. Discharges via @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.
# eigenform_witnessing on o.witness — the recursion has a fixed
# point.
#
# Presupposes depth_at_least(3, o). Required by third_order_active.
# Grounded in Lawvere fixed-point theorem via
# @epistemologic/math/lawvere.is_autopoietic (per boot/std/cogito.
# mirror precedent).
recursion_folds_back(o: observation_depth) -> verdict { \ }

# === mechanism_visible(o) predicate ===
#
# The Loki requirement: the observed structure is legible under the
# reflexivity carrier. Discharges via a threshold check on o.
# reflexivity — the substrate-pull discipline requires the mechanism
# under observation to be inspectable.
#
# This predicate surfaced during writing of the canonical spec
# (§10.3 circular-reflexive noticing). Without it, the substrate
# could witness depth-3 recursion without the mechanism being
# legible, defeating Loki's structural claim. The predicate lifts
# the mechanism-visibility requirement to substrate-decl.
#
# "This piece knows it is doing what it describes" is the
# structural version: the observation must know what it is
# observing at a level the substrate can verify.
mechanism_visible(o: observation_depth) -> verdict { \ }

# === third_order_active(o) composed bilateral ===
#
# The load-bearing bilateral. Discharges four sub-predicates over
# observation_depth. Consumers cite this in `requires` clauses when
# they need the substrate to verify depth-3 discipline at the
# boundary.
#
# Composition per the substrate's composed-bilateral discipline
# (StageFreight-shape from @io/stagefreight; Shatter-shape from
# @smarts/shatter; @reflection third_order_coherent shape from
# reflection-third-order-by-default-v0.1.md §5). Four sub-predicates
# projecting onto the carrier fields; all must hold for the
# composed verdict to pass.
#
# Failure modes surface via transparency<observation_depth> per
# @glass discipline (spec §7.2):
#   fail depth_at_least              -> partial(o.depth / 3)
#   fail observer_observes_observing -> Fail(missing_second_order)
#   fail recursion_folds_back        -> Fail(open_recursion)
#   fail mechanism_visible           -> partial(reflexivity_pct)
third_order_active(o: observation_depth) -> verdict { \ }

# === witness_third_order action ===
#
# The typed constructor. Any family that opts in via `in @third`
# uses this action to produce depth-3 observation carriers. The
# postcondition `requires third_order_active(result)` enforces the
# discipline at the boundary — the substrate refuses to settle if
# any of the four sub-predicates fails.
#
# primary  = what is being observed (a substrate ref)
# observer = who is observing (the depth-2 machinery)
# meta     = what observes the observing (the depth-3 machinery)
#
# Species-refinement per family (forward-promised):
#   @reflection.third_order_observation <: observation_depth
#   @cogito.cognitive_third_order       <: observation_depth
#   @pack.multi_repo_third_order        <: observation_depth
#   @cyberpunk.recursion_lock_third_order <: observation_depth
#   @fate.tournament_third_order        <: observation_depth
#   @cascade.cascade_third_order        <: observation_depth
witness_third_order(primary: ref, observer: ref, meta: ref)
  -> observation_depth
requires third_order_active(result)
{ \ }

out @third
out observation_depth
out depth_at_least
out observer_observes_observing
out recursion_folds_back
out mechanism_visible
out third_order_active
out witness_third_order
